From: Austin Schuh <austin.schuh@bluerivertech.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse _MPN_ARCH select for gmp_config_m4

The inline select() inside gmp_config_m4 only mapped a small handful of
@platforms//cpu:* values to gmp arch names ("aarch64", "arm", "powerpc64",
"s390_64", "x86_64"). Every other arch -- including the very common
@platforms//cpu:armv7, @platforms//cpu:arm64, @platforms//cpu:arm64e,
@platforms//cpu:i386, @platforms//cpu:x86_32, @platforms//cpu:mips64,
@platforms//cpu:ppc32, @platforms//cpu:riscv32/64 -- fell through to
"generic".

The "generic" config.m4 emits ELF-flavoured `.type sym,@function` and
omits the per-arch *-defs.m4 includes. On ARM this is fatal: `@` is the
ARM assembler line-comment character, so `.type sym,@function` becomes
`.type sym,` and gas fails with `unrecognized symbol type ""`. The
missing arm-defs.m4 also leaves macros like `return` and the `C`
single-line-comment marker untouched, producing additional assembler
errors like `bad instruction 'return r14'` and
`garbage following instruction -- '... C return value'`.

The rest of the build (_MPN_ARCH, _MPN_ASM_SRCS, gmp_mparam_h) already
maps all of these constraint_values correctly. Reuse _MPN_ARCH for
gmp_config_m4 so the config.m4 stays in sync with everything else.

Tested on a 32-bit ARM (roborio, armv7) toolchain, where this fixes
assembly compilation of mpn/*.s for gmp 6.3.0.
---
 BUILD.bazel | 9 +--------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -746,14 +746,7 @@
 
 gmp_config_m4(
     name = "config_m4",
-    arch = select({
-        "@platforms//cpu:aarch64": "aarch64",
-        "@platforms//cpu:arm": "arm",
-        "@platforms//cpu:ppc64le": "powerpc64",
-        "@platforms//cpu:s390x": "s390_64",
-        "@platforms//cpu:x86_64": "x86_64",
-        "//conditions:default": "generic",
-    }),
+    arch = _MPN_ARCH,
     mparam_h = ":gmp_mparam_h",
     os = select({
         "@platforms//os:linux": "linux",
